{"subject": "maths", "level": "ibdp", "topic_display": "Number & Algebra", "topic_slug": "number--algebra", "theme": "maths-grid", "adventure_n": 2, "title": "Sequences, Series and Sigma Notation", "emoji": "➕", "welcome_lead": "Explore arithmetic and geometric progressions and the elegant Σ notation for sums.", "meta_desc": "Maths adventure on arithmetic and geometric sequences, series, and sigma notation.", "final_note": "Sequences power finance, physics and infinite sums!", "concepts": [{"term": "Arithmetic sequence", "def": "u_n = u_1 + (n-1)d, constant difference d."}, {"term": "Geometric sequence", "def": "u_n = u_1 × r^(n-1), constant ratio r."}, {"term": "Arithmetic sum", "def": "S_n = n/2 × (2u_1 + (n-1)d)."}, {"term": "Geometric sum", "def": "S_n = u_1(1-r^n)/(1-r) for r ≠ 1."}, {"term": "Infinite sum", "def": "S_∞ = u_1/(1-r) requires |r| < 1."}, {"term": "Sigma notation", "def": "Σ from i=1 to n of a_i is a compact sum."}], "walkthroughs": [{"tag": "ap", "h2": "Arithmetic Sum", "body_html": "<p>Find S_20 for u_1 = 3, d = 4.</p><p>S_20 = 20/2 × (2(3) + 19(4)) = 10 × (6 + 76) = 820.</p>"}, {"tag": "gp", "h2": "Geometric Sum", "body_html": "<p>Sum 2 + 6 + 18 +. for 8 terms.</p><p>r = 3, so S_8 = 2(1 - 3^8)/(1-3) = 2(1-6561)/(-2) = 6560.</p>"}, {"tag": "sigma", "h2": "Sigma Notation", "body_html": "<p>Evaluate Σ from k=1 to 5 of (2k+1).</p><p>= 3 + 5 + 7 + 9 + 11 = 35.</p>"}], "mcqs": [{"q": "Formula for the nth term of an arithmetic sequence?", "options": [["u_1 + (n-1)d", 1], ["u_1 × r^(n-1)", 0], ["u_1 + nd", 0], ["u_1 × r^n", 0]]}, {"q": "When does an infinite geometric series converge?", "options": [["|r| < 1", 1], ["|r| > 1", 0], ["r = 1", 0], ["r > 0", 0]]}], "numericals": [{"q": "Sum to infinity of 8 + 4 + 2 + 1 +.?", "options": [12, 14, 16, 20], "answer": 16}], "free_texts": [{"q": "What Greek letter denotes summation?", "answer": "sigma"}]}